{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the Tent of Meeting shall set out — in the midst of the camps.</b> Between the two standards mentioned." "<b>As they encamp, so shall they set out.</b> For when half of all the standards have set out, the Mishkan will be fully erected in the middle of all of them, because immediately after the standard of Reuben came the Kohathites, bearers of the sanctuary — which is the principal of the מועד — as it says: וְנוֹעַדְתִּי לְךָ שָׁם וְדִבַּרְתִּי אִתְּךָ מֵעַל הַכַּפֹּרֶת (Exodus 25:22)." "<b>As they encamp.</b> And so it was then in the midst of all the camps, even at the time of the journey."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The logic: by the time the second standard (Reuben) has departed, the Kohathites follow bearing the already-disassembled sanctuary components; thus when the camp halts, the Mishkan is re-erected precisely in the center."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:31.767284645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}